### Key changes:

**`MarkdownViewer.vue`**
- Added a custom `fence` renderer that detects code blocks with a file path in their info string (e.g. ` ```js src/foo/bar.js `)
- Wraps matching blocks in a `<div id="...">` with an anchor ID derived from the file path, prefixed by `documentId`

**`DocumentSummary.vue`**
- Rewrote heading extraction to properly track code fence nesting (so heading-like lines inside plain code blocks are ignored)
- Code blocks with a file path (` ```lang file/path `) are extracted as TOC entries at level 2 with a 📄 icon
- The anchor slug generation mirrors the one used in `MarkdownViewer` so links resolve correctly
